  designNotes: 'Beat 10: a clock, and the beat chart names its length - "armor in
    2 turns". Default is 6 rifle + 2 machine gunners so the volley can cover the yard
    AND the arriving column. The lead is 2 rather than 1 for that reason: one turn is a heads-up
    you can only brace for, two is long enough to change what you are shooting at
    and still have a volley left to do it with, which is the whole "kill priority
    vs clock" beat. The strip counts down live (2 turns, then 1 turn) because a warning
    holding the same number for two turns says the clock has stopped. This is the
    first level in the project to fire a ReinforcementWave; its telegraph and announcement
    were imported and displayed nowhere from the port until Phase F. WAVE MOVED 2026-08-12: at anchorX 9 the nearest of the four heavies stood
    0.09 inside GarrisonPost''s box and could not be hit. Moved to 9.4, which clears the box edge
    by 0.31 and keeps the deepest man at dx 20.06 from the back rank, just inside the 20.25 flat
    envelope. Found by extending rule 8 to mid-battle arrivals.'
